      "stepKey": "two-three-shift",
      "stepKind": "polar",
      "toStateId": "alkoxide",
      "fromStateId": "carbanion",
      "canonicalArrows": [
        "lp C1 -> σ C1-C5",
        "π C4-C5 -> π C3-C4",
        "σ O2-C3 -> lp O2"
      ],
      "routePreference": "preferred",
      "explanationAfterStep": "A [2,3]-sigmatropic shift through an envelope-shaped five-membered transition state: six electrons (the lone pair, the π bond and the C–O σ bond) move round five atoms. A C–O bond and a carbanion are traded for a C–C bond and an alkoxide, so the step is downhill. The allyl group is attached at its far end, so a substituted allyl group is transposed. With a substituted allyl group, the envelope transition state sets the relative configuration of the two new stereocentres. The app does not check stereochemistry yet, so the drawings carry no wedges and no E/Z marks."
    },
