  "mechanismSummary": "In the [2,3]-Wittig rearrangement (not to be confused with the Wittig alkene synthesis), an allyl ether is deprotonated next to oxygen, here by butyllithium at the benzylic position. The carbanion attacks the far end of the allyl group through a five-membered, envelope-shaped transition state while the O–allyl bond breaks: a [2,3]-sigmatropic shift giving a homoallylic alkoxide. It needs low temperature; on warming, the competing [1,2]-Wittig rearrangement (via a radical pair) takes over. The app does not check stereochemistry yet, so the drawings carry no wedges and no E/Z marks.",
